  "explains": "requestLog in src/middleware/requestLog.ts prints the address. src/app.ts imports it and registers it with app.use(requestLog), a statement that runs for every request the app answers and that is not a route: what it reaches cannot be narrowed to a route, and undecidable means affected, so every route of the app is reached, in the file and through its mounts: the fifteen routes of the service. (The registration order and a path prefix are not evaluated.) The client calls six of them: ORDERS_URL, orderUrl, customerOrdersUrl, customerUrl, ADMIN_STATS_URL and INVOICES_URL, so six http edges and four screens: /orders, /orders/:orderId, /customers/:customerId and /stats. Nothing of the ledger service is reached: it is another repository and no edge leads from here to it.",
